{"nodes": [{"id": "packages_docs_docs_architecture_event_stream_four_layer_model", "label": "Event-Stream Four-Layer Model", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Separates source representations, the event-stream contract, listeners/writers, and the retained naturalized representation so readers, writers, naturalizers, validators, and anonymizers all compose on one contract.", "source_file": "packages/docs/docs/architecture/event-stream.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_docs_docs_architecture_event_stream_contract", "label": "Event-Stream Contract (Hybrid Push Core)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The contract is a synchronous push core with an async-iterator adapter layered on top: the push core keeps the hot path allocation-free, the adapter offers for-await ergonomics. Backpressure is applied out of band (setDrain/awaitDrain) only at defined checkpoints.", "source_file": "packages/docs/docs/architecture/event-stream.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_docs_docs_architecture_event_stream_loss_preservation", "label": "Loss Preservation Invariant", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A generator emits every observed value and item regardless of declared VM; cardinality enforcement and diagnostics are listener policies, never the stream's, keeping the stream purely loss-preserving.", "source_file": "packages/docs/docs/architecture/event-stream.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_docs_docs_architecture_event_stream_source_agnostic_equivalence", "label": "Source-Agnostic Equivalence", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Because all sources emit the same contract, the naturalized object is identical across origins; verified across the fixture corpus by naturalizing each fixture from raw